From bb6aad439935f66b6836100af217c629aaf83eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:24:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] base-files: leave the service cgroup before stopping it

B76, from openwrt/openwrt#26470 (branch b76-rc-common-cgroup) as it stands, its
PKG_RELEASE changes replaced by the port's own bumps.

Since procd 39b5aac8c1 ("service: clean up descendant processes for
non-jail instances"), procd kills what is left in an instance's cgroup
when its main process exits. A restart run from inside the service runs
in that cgroup: its stop takes the shell running it with it, and the
start after it never runs. restart() ignores SIGTERM across its stop
for this case, but the cgroup is killed with SIGKILL.

A shell over SSH runs in dropbear's cgroup, so
`/etc/init.d/dropbear restart` from an SSH session leaves dropbear
stopped, and the device unreachable over SSH until a reboot. A daemon
that restarts its own service, as after an update, stays stopped the
same way.

Before procd_kill, move the shell to the root cgroup when it is in the
cgroup of the service it stops.

Tested on an Arista W-118 (ipq40xx, procd 0d3c5dc1), with a second
dropbear on port 2222 as its own procd service:
- before: its restart from a session on port 2222 closed the session,
  and port 2222 stayed refused, the service gone from procd.
- after: the session closed, and port 2222 took a new session 6 s
  later.
A test daemon that runs its own service's restart never came back
before, and came back with a new PID after, twice in a row.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/base-files/files/etc/rc.common | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/base-files/files/etc/rc.common b/package/base-files/files/etc/rc.common
index abf72ea3372..1a4a9fea6b1 100755
--- a/package/base-files/files/etc/rc.common
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/rc.common
@@ -153,9 +153,19 @@ extra_command "enabled" "Check if service is started on boot"
 		_procd_ubus_call list
 	}
 
+	# procd kills what is left in an instance's cgroup when the instance
+	# exits: leave the service's cgroup before stopping it, so that a
+	# restart run from inside the service lives on to start it again
+	_procd_leave_cgroup() {
+		grep -qs "^0::/services/$1/" /proc/$$/cgroup &&
+			echo $$ > /sys/fs/cgroup/cgroup.procs 2>/dev/null
+		return 0
+	}
+
 	stop() {
 		procd_lock
 		stop_service "$@"
+		_procd_leave_cgroup "$(basename ${basescript:-$initscript})"
 		procd_kill "$(basename ${basescript:-$initscript})" "$1"
 		if eval "type service_stopped" 2>/dev/null >/dev/null; then
 			service_stopped
-- 
